From 0d5a19c80776f9ef62386665c37732bd7f755ff6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeongik Cha <jeongik@google.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 02:44:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gfxstream: support variable descriptor counts and sparse
 DescriptorWriteTable

When a descriptor set layout binding uses
VK_DESCRIPTOR_BINDING_VARIABLE_DESCRIPTOR_COUNT_BIT, its descriptorCount
specifies an upper bound, while the actual number of descriptors
allocated for a set comes from
VkDescriptorSetVariableDescriptorCountAllocateInfo (or 0 if omitted).

Track VkDescriptorSetLayoutBindingFlagsCreateInfo on the guest
DescriptorSetLayoutInfo, resolve the effective variable descriptor count
during pool validation, pool accounting, and ReifiedDescriptorSet
initialization, and allocate variable-count descriptor sets
synchronously through enc->vkAllocateDescriptorSets even when
hasVulkanBatchedDescriptorSetUpdate is enabled so Cereal marshals
VkDescriptorSetVariableDescriptorCountAllocateInfo natively without
custom pendingAllocations bit-packing. Track allocatedFromPoolIds on
ReifiedDescriptorSet so synchronously allocated sets are never pushed
into preallocated freePoolIds on free or pool reset, and widen
DescriptorPoolAllocationInfo::allocedPoolIds to uint64_t so 64-bit box
poolId handles are not truncated on insertion.

Also replace the dense std::vector<DescriptorBindingElementWrite> in
DescriptorWriteTable with a sparse std::unordered_map keyed by
descriptor array element index, guard per-set mutations with a mutex on
ReifiedDescriptorSet and descriptor pool/set/layout lifecycle mutations
with ResourceTracker::mLock, and track per-binding dirtyIndices so
commitDescriptorSetUpdates flushes only newly modified entries in
O(dirty) time while preserving written elements for subsequent
VkCopyDescriptorSet emulation.

https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45927

Signed-off-by: Jeongik Cha <jeongik@google.com>
